<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kitab al-Farq</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Book of the Difference</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kitob">Kitab</a> al-Farq, or Book of the Difference, is a political treatise by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usman-dan-fodio">Usman dan Fodio</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>. It contrasts just Islamic government with the practices of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> rulers he opposed. Together with his other writings it provided the ideological framework of Sokoto governance, setting Islamic law as the standard by which rulers were judged.</p></div>
